{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function batch<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/batcher.ts#L323","children":[{"type":"text","value":"batcher.ts:323"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a batcher that processes items in batches."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncBatch when you need promises, retry support, abort/cancel capabilities, or advanced error handling."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/BatcherOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BatcherOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(item): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adds an item to the batcher\nIf the batch size is reached, timeout occurs, or shouldProcess returns true, the batch will be processed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"item","children":[{"type":"text","value":"item"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const batchItems = batch<number>(\n  (items) => console.log('Processing:', items),\n  {\n    maxSize: 3,\n    onExecute: (batch, batcher) => console.log('Batch executed:', batch)\n  }\n);\n\nbatchItems(1);\nbatchItems(2);\nbatchItems(3); // Triggers batch processing","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"item","text":"item","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction batch<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [batcher.ts:323](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/batcher.ts#L323)\n\nCreates a batcher that processes items in batches.\n\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncBatch when you need promises, retry support, abort/cancel capabilities, or advanced error handling.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `void`\n\n### options\n\n[`BatcherOptions`](../interfaces/BatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(item): void;\n```\n\nAdds an item to the batcher\nIf the batch size is reached, timeout occurs, or shouldProcess returns true, the batch will be processed\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### item\n\n`TValue`\n\n### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst batchItems = batch<number>(\n  (items) => console.log('Processing:', items),\n  {\n    maxSize: 3,\n    onExecute: (batch, batcher) => console.log('Batch executed:', batch)\n  }\n);\n\nbatchItems(1);\nbatchItems(2);\nbatchItems(3); // Triggers batch processing\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: batch\ntitle: batch\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction batch<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [batcher.ts:323](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/batcher.ts#L323)\n\nCreates a batcher that processes items in batches.\n\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncBatch when you need promises, retry support, abort/cancel capabilities, or advanced error handling.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `void`\n\n### options\n\n[`BatcherOptions`](../interfaces/BatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(item): void;\n```\n\nAdds an item to the batcher\nIf the batch size is reached, timeout occurs, or shouldProcess returns true, the batch will be processed\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### item\n\n`TValue`\n\n### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst batchItems = batch<number>(\n  (items) => console.log('Processing:', items),\n  {\n    maxSize: 3,\n    onExecute: (batch, batcher) => console.log('Batch executed:', batch)\n  }\n);\n\nbatchItems(1);\nbatchItems(2);\nbatchItems(3); // Triggers batch processing\n```\n"}
